From: TB710FU clean board
Subject: [PATCH] Put the ramoops console region inside the managed memory span

The 0004 ramoops patch targets physical 0xac340000, which is 32.3 GiB below
gPhysBase 0x8c0000000 and outside the 2 GiB owned window
[0x8c0000000, 0x940000000). ml_io_map cannot describe it, so the console zone
was never written - which is why every pstore read came back empty.

This moves the default region to 0x93ff00000, 256 KiB, 16 KiB aligned, 1 MiB
below the top of the window so it avoids the identity-mapped switch-marker page
at 0x93ffff000 introduced by 0007. That leaves roughly 1.88 GiB of headroom in
the span and no overlap with the kernel image, boot args, device tree, page
tables or the appended __KDIAG segment.

A ramoops=<PA> boot argument still overrides the default, but only when the
supplied address lies inside the span with room for the zone; out-of-span values
(specifically the live 0xac340000) are rejected so an unreachable address cannot
be selected silently. The zone is now enabled by default; ramoops_size,
ramoops_ecc, ramoops_panic_delay, ramoops_reset_after, ramoops_reset_warm and
ramoops_selftest keep their existing behaviour.

Source: osfmk/kern/tb710fu_ramoops.c after 0004. Generated from the real source
lines so the hunk applies cleanly. 0008 only touches ramoops.c, while 0005-0007
touch arm_vm_init.c, so the file sets are disjoint.

Boundary: tb710fu_ramoops_init() runs after arm_vm_init() returns. It therefore
cannot capture a stop inside arm_vm_init (stage 47); 0007's identity-mapped
markers cover that. 0008 establishes the durable console channel for boots that
get past the switch, and fixes the "address reachable at all" problem.
diff --git a/osfmk/kern/tb710fu_ramoops.c b/osfmk/kern/tb710fu_ramoops.c
--- a/osfmk/kern/tb710fu_ramoops.c
+++ b/osfmk/kern/tb710fu_ramoops.c
@@ -275,13 +275,30 @@ tb710fu_ramoops_init(void)
 void
 tb710fu_ramoops_init(void)
 {
-	uint64_t pa = 0;
-	uint32_t size = 0x40000, ecc = 16;
-
-	if (!PE_parse_boot_argn("ramoops", &pa, sizeof(pa)) || pa == 0) {
-		early_len = sizeof(early);  /* disabled: stop buffering */
-		return;
-	}
+	/*
+	 * TB710FU: the Android ramoops zone at 0xac340000 is 32.3 GiB below
+	 * gPhysBase (0x8c0000000) and cannot be reached by ml_io_map. Reserve
+	 * a 256 KiB region inside the managed span instead. It sits 1 MiB below
+	 * the top of the 2 GiB window so it does not collide with the 0007
+	 * switch-marker page at 0x93ffff000. See docs/LOG_REGION_IN_WINDOW.md.
+	 */
+#define TB710FU_LOG_REGION_PA    0x93ff00000ULL
+#define TB710FU_LOG_REGION_SIZE  0x40000U
+#define TB710FU_SPAN_BASE        0x8c0000000ULL
+#define TB710FU_SPAN_END         0x940000000ULL
+
+	uint64_t pa = TB710FU_LOG_REGION_PA;
+	uint64_t arg_pa = 0;
+	uint32_t size = TB710FU_LOG_REGION_SIZE, ecc = 16;
+
+	/* A boot-arg override is honoured only when it names an in-span range.
+	 * The live argument 0xac340000 is out of span and falls back to the
+	 * default instead of silently selecting an unreachable address. */
+	if (PE_parse_boot_argn("ramoops", &arg_pa, sizeof(arg_pa)) &&
+	    arg_pa >= TB710FU_SPAN_BASE &&
+	    arg_pa + size <= TB710FU_SPAN_END) {
+		pa = arg_pa;
+	}
 	PE_parse_boot_argn("ramoops_size", &size, sizeof(size));
 	PE_parse_boot_argn("ramoops_ecc", &ecc, sizeof(ecc));
 	PE_parse_boot_argn("ramoops_panic_delay", &panic_delay, sizeof(panic_delay));
